# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is committed. This workspace ships binaries — the shell and the
# sample platform — and for a binary the lockfile is what makes a build
# reproducible: without it, two people cloning a week apart compile different
# dependency trees and only one of them has the bug. The rule that lockfiles are
# noise applies to libraries, whose dependents resolve their own.

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Test artifacts
/tmp/
/test-results/

# Database files
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Coverage reports
/coverage/
tarpaulin-report.html
cobertura.xml
lcov.info

# Build artifacts
**/*.orig

# Metis ephemeral state
.metis/.index-dirty

# Documentation build output
/site/

# Generated API docs (plissken render; regenerated by `angreal docs api` and CI)
/docs/api/rust/
/docs/api/_nav.yml

# Environment
.env
.env.local
demo/state/
# Built frontends, one per design pack.
examples/*/dist/

# Local Claude Code session state
.claude/

# Python bytecode from angreal tasks
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Browser tests
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/screenshots/
e2e/report/
e2e/results/

# Vendored crates build in place when used outside the workspace. Their target
# directory and their lockfile are both artefacts of that build, in a tree that
# is not ours to keep tidy.
vendor/*/target/
vendor/*/Cargo.lock
